do MouseManager.set_mouse_mode_visible()
Intercom: Attention all players the game will now begin
[i]The previously locked door automatically opens[/i]
Intercom: Anyone who refuses to participate will be automatically disqualified. Any disqualified players are automatically eliminated
[i]Everyone hurries through the door[/i]
[i]Inside you find 5 platforms and 5 pillars with a screen on top[/i]
Intercom: All players must stand on their assigned platform
[i]You look around and find a pillar with your name on it. The others do the same. You stand on the platform and look at the screen on the pillar.[/i]
[i] Right at that moment the rest of the floor retracts into the wall. You look down and all you can see is a dark pit.[/i]
Jock: What the hell!??
Intercom: Players will now direct their attention to their screens.
[i]On the screen you can see an icon representing the five other players. Beneath each icon are three hearts.[/i]
Intercom: The rules are simple. You will all vote for one other player. Each time a player is voted for they will lose a life. The first player to lose all three lives will be eliminated.
Intercom: After the votes are cast, but before they are revealed, you have the option to dodge. If you correctly guess which other player has voted for you, you can dodge their vote nullifying it. Guess wrong, and you will lose a heart.
Intercom: You only get one dodge per round of voting. Voting continues until someone is eliminated. First round of voting begins in 5 minutes
[i]Five minutes isn't a lot of time but it might be enough to convince someone else not to vote for you.[/i]
- Convince Artsy
	jump gameplay_artsy_round_1/
- Convince Jock
	jump gameplay_jock_round_1/
- Convince Mean
	jump gameplay_mean_round_1/
- Convince Nice
	jump gameplay_nice_round_1/
- Convince Nerd
	jump gameplay_nerd_round_1/
- Don't try to convince anyone
	jump gameplay_round_1/
do MouseManager.set_mouse_mode_captured()